{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>To encamp you.</b> It is not a transitive verb, for we do not find this binyan used thus." "<b>To search out for you.</b> The lamed is opened [with pataḥ] to indicate that the letter is heh, heh — the knowledge that is absent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The lemma לחנותכם (\"to encamp you\") is Ibn Ezra's grammatical puzzle: the hif'il of חנה with a pronominal suffix would make it transitive, but he notes this binyan is not found as transitive."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:55.092304588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}